# User note outranks description

In this extension, a human **User note** (`inputs.user_note`, `USER-NOTE.md`) **outranks** **description** (`state.json` description, Change `requirement.desiredOutcome`, Jira / GitHub / Drive / URL ticket body).

When they conflict, follow the user note. Fold both into the requirement artifact. Do not skip the note. Do not discard the source description.

## Product surfaces

- Start Epic / New Change: User note sits above description; copy must say it wins on conflict.
- Epic detail / Owning change: show User note first, then source description — never dump only the composed blob as "Mô tả".
- Agent skills, slash commands, provider-managed task, run feedback: include `USER_NOTE_PRIORITY_RULE` from `composeRequirementWithUserNote.ts`.
- Mark-done on `REQUIREMENT.md` still gates on user-note coverage.

## cofofo-feature analyze artifacts

- Gated Canvas file: `docs/epics/{epic}/artifacts/REQUIREMENT.md` only.
- Required headings include screens / screen flow / APIs / API flow plus `## 9. Research / citations` and `## 10. Options & task decisions`.
- Discover `REQUIREMENTS.md` (product) is not the epic `REQUIREMENT.md` (task).
- `OPTIONS.md` / `EVIDENCE.md` / `TASK-DECISIONS.md` are leftover from a retired analyze split. If they exist, fold into §§ 9–10. They are not pipeline artifacts. Do not write them as the requirement.

## Do not

- Treat `description` as the primary brief when a user note exists.
- Tell the agent to wait for Jira MCP instead of reading `USER-NOTE.md` + `inputs.json`.
- Gate analyze Canvas on `OPTIONS.md` / `EVIDENCE.md` / `TASK-DECISIONS.md`.
- Treat leftover research files as sacred or as a second requirement source.
